  "description": "Verifies that sign(y_λ) equals sign(Z)·(−1)^P(λ), where P(λ) counts cells of λ whose content lies below c* = −log_Q(Q^r). Derived from the Wenzl principal specialisation: for Q>1 every hook factor 1−Q^h is negative (fixed sign (−1)^|λ|), and a numerator factor 1−Q^r·Q^c is negative exactly above the threshold. Swept over every partition for n=2..12. Replaces the qualitative 'sign-indefinite for n≥4' of weight-factor-audit §W3 with a combinatorial rule, which is what makes the μ₃ door budget of PR #4657 computable.",
